  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P2] Restore precomputed ID lookup — remapping `current` per element is O(n·m)",
      "body": "`current.map(candidate => candidate.id)` now executes inside the `.filter()` predicate, so for `n = previous.length` and `m = current.length` the function performs `n·m` ID reads plus `n` throwaway `m`-element array allocations, versus the removed version's O(n+m) time with one O(m) `Set`. For a reconcile-style function over, say, 10,000×10,000 items this is ~100M comparisons and 10,000 intermediate arrays — significant latency and GC pressure on the synchronous path. The repository contains no callers or tests establishing that inputs are always small. Hoist the ID collection once (ideally back into a `Set` for O(1) membership).",
      "severity": "P2",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/reconcile.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 42,
        "end": 42
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Inline nested `map().includes()` obscures the membership-test intent",
      "body": "The doubly-nested inline expression reads as a transformation chain rather than what it is — a membership test against the set of current IDs. The removed named intermediate (`currentIds`) made the predicate's meaning and expected lookup cost immediately clear to readers.",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/reconcile.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 42,
        "end": 42
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Changed function has no test coverage",
      "body": "`removedIds` is the only real code in the file and this rewrite touches its entire body, yet the repository has no tests for it, so equivalence (empty inputs, overlapping IDs, duplicates, IDs absent from `current`) is unverified by anything executable. Adding a small unit test would pin the contract this PR claims to preserve.",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/reconcile.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 41,
        "end": 43
      }
    }
  ],
